NAME
    sort - sort lines of text

SYNOPSIS
    sort [-n] [-r] [text...]

DESCRIPTION
    Sorts lines from piped standard input (or trailing literal [text...]
    joined by spaces). By default, lines are ordered by UTF-8 code-point
    (ordinal) comparison. Combine with uniq(1) ('sort | uniq') to remove
    duplicates.

OPTIONS
    -n  Parse each trimmed line as a 64-bit floating-point number (f64)
        and sort numerically; lines that do not parse as numbers sort as
        0.0.
    -r  Reverse the sort order.

EXAMPLES
    watch list | sort -n
    cat /Logs/names.txt | sort -r | uniq

EXIT STATUS
    0   Always succeeds.

SEE ALSO
    uniq(1), grep(1), awk(1)
